Imagine if you will, two men with military experience, all the maturity that you expect to see, but here they are playing on a television screen with all the intensity as though their life's prestige depends upon it. That's the way it was in that 10 by 20 room.

734
02:25:02,211 --> 02:25:11,211
Ralph's bosses gave him over $2,000 for staff and $500 for parts, so Ralph could develop the game box further.

735
02:25:11,211 --> 02:25:18,211
Imagine that, the video game revolution began on $2,500 worth of R&D money.

736
02:25:20,211 --> 02:25:27,211
Ralph's TV game box became the Magnavox Odyssey, the world's first home video game console.

737
02:25:28,211 --> 02:25:31,211
Magnavox presents Odyssey, the electronic game of the future.

738
02:25:32,211 --> 02:25:40,211
It arrived in the shops in 1972, and over the next decade, Ralph's idea transformed the home entertainment business.

739
02:25:41,211 --> 02:25:49,211
I don't think he would have dreamed that he was creating an industry that would be in the billions of dollars by this time today.

740
02:25:52,211 --> 02:26:00,211
In 2006, Ralph received the prestigious National Medal of Technology in honor of his video game inventions from the US president.

